# Pixelanea Frontend Practices

Full reference: [PRACTICES.md](../../PRACTICES.md) · Skill: `.cursor/skills/pixelanea-frontend-standards/`

## Layers (`apps/web/src`)

```text
pages/ → shell/, components/, canvas/
shell/ → header, layout, tool rail, palette slot, frame strip (hidden if frameCount ≤ 1)
components/{toolbar,palette,frames,animation,project,import,onboarding}/
components/ui/ → Radix + CVA primitives (no store imports)
canvas/ + tools/ → commands; coordinates in canvas/ only
state/ → editorStore, uiStore, sessionStore, shortcuts.ts
content/ → all user-facing strings
api/ → generated OpenAPI wrappers
styles/ → tokens.css, theme.css
```

## Chrome vs viewport

- **Chrome:** `accent`, Outfit, panels — [DESIGN.md](../../DESIGN.md)
- **Viewport:** `checker-a`, `grid-line`, user swatches only — no brand greens on pixels
- Single `<canvas>` — no DOM per pixel

## Rules

1. **No backend leakage** — no SQLite, ZIP, blob encoding, or hand-rolled fetch DTOs.
2. **Two front doors** — blank canvas and import wizard are equal entry paths ([UX.md](../../UX.md)).
3. **Tool plugin model** — new edits = `Tool` + `Command`; register in `tools/`.
4. **Progressive disclosure** — frame strip when `frameCount > 1`; technical info opt-in.
5. **Confirm sparingly** — only delete, overwrite, duplicate frames, remove in-use color.
6. **Copy in `content/`** — plain language; no error codes or emoji toasts.
7. **Accessibility** — icon + label on tools; active state = accent + 3px left border + weight.

## Before merging

- [ ] Generated client types for all API calls
- [ ] Coordinate math only in `canvas/`
- [ ] `readOnly` honored during playback
- [ ] Design tokens for chrome; functional tokens for canvas
- [ ] Shared debounced autosave path
- [ ] OpenAPI updated if contract changed
